-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## Learning Objectives
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC By the end of this lesson, you will be able to:
-- MAGIC - Configure and register external storage locations with Unity Catalog
-- MAGIC - Override managed storage locations to isolate data between catalogs
-- MAGIC - Replace legacy DBFS mounts with modern Unity Catalog external location patterns

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## A. External Storage Integration with Unity Catalog
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Unity Catalog connects to external cloud storage through two key components:
-- MAGIC - **Storage credentials** form the "gateway" to a particular cloud storage container by encapsulating the authentication information
-- MAGIC - **External locations** augment a storage credential by providing a construct that represents a subpath within the cloud storage container
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Each component can be individually access-controlled, and together they provide fine-grained access control over external data sources.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### A1. Storage Credentials
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Storage credentials constitute the fundamental component of connecting Unity Catalog to external storage. You cannot access external data without one.
-- MAGIC
