-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">ℹ️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       The <code>CREATE STORAGE CREDENTIAL</code> and <code>CREATE EXTERNAL LOCATION</code> privileges allow non-admin users to create storage credentials and external locations, respectively. Using these, this storage admin capability can be delegated as a separate role if desired (as reflected in the diagram above).
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC #### A2.2 Creating External Locations
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Creating external locations can be done interactively through the **Catalog Explorer** user interface or via a SQL command. In this section, we'll create one using each method; one for the finance organization and one for the engineering team.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Before proceeding, please ensure you have:
-- MAGIC - a unique base name (in the metastore) for your external locations
-- MAGIC - the base location of the cloud storage managed by the storage credential you created in the previous section

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ##### A2.2.1 Create External Locations in the UI
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Let's create an external location for non-production use, using the UI.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. From **Catalog Explorer**, select **Connect &gt; External Locations**.
-- MAGIC 1. In the **External Locations** tab, click **Create external location**.
-- MAGIC 1. Fill in a unique **External location name**, using the base name you chose, adding the suffix `-dev`.
-- MAGIC 1. Select the appropriate **Storage type** (for example, *S3*).
-- MAGIC 1. Specify the cloud storage URL. This should include the base path of the storage container, plus a subpath within that container (for this example, add `/dev`).
-- MAGIC 1. Select the **Storage Credential** that you created previously.
-- MAGIC 1. Click **Create**.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ##### A2.2.2 Create External Locations using SQL
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Paste the following command into a notebook or SQL editor, adjusting values to reflect:
-- MAGIC - the base name you chose (with the `-prd` suffix)
-- MAGIC - the cloud storage URL, including the base path with the suffix `/prd`
-- MAGIC - the name of the storage credential to associate this external location with 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div class="code-block" data-language="sql">
-- MAGIC CREATE EXTERNAL LOCATION `{external location base name}-prd`
-- MAGIC URL '{storage container base URL}/prd'
-- MAGIC WITH (STORAGE CREDENTIAL {name of storage credential})
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <link href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/prism/1.29.0/themes/prism.min.css" rel="stylesheet" />
