-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC #### B3.2 DBFS Mount Migration
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Since UC itself does not model a file system, it doesn't support the concept of direct mounting like DBFS did. Instead, we need to map DBFS mounts using the constructs that allow UC to reach external storage: storage credentials and external locations.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. For each unique storage container identified in the previous section (in this exaple there were the *acme-landing* and *acme-analytics* buckets), create a storage credential connecting Unity Catalog to that container.
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #1976d2; background: #e3f2fd; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">ℹ️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       This will require policy reconfiguration, and obtaining the ARN of the container, as outlined earlier in this demo.
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC 1. Create external locations as needed associated with the storage credentials created in the previous step.
-- MAGIC    - At a minimum, create one external location per storage credential.
-- MAGIC    - In situations where multiple mounts refer to the same bucket, create multiple external locations associated with the same underlying storage credential.
-- MAGIC 1. Determine where (catalog and schema) and how (table or volume) the data will be integrated into Unity Catalog.
-- MAGIC    - By default, files can be mapped in using a **volume**.
-- MAGIC    - If the data files at location represent structured data files in a supported format, consider mapping it in as a **table**.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #1976d2; background: #e3f2fd; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">ℹ️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       In either case, the object will be <strong>external</strong> (not managed), since the underlying data resides outside the managed storage location.
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC The command below illustrates how to create an external volume referencing one of the example locations from above.
-- MAGIC <div class="code-block" data-language="sql">
-- MAGIC CREATE EXTERNAL VOLUME acme_landing
-- MAGIC   LOCATION 's3a://acme-landing/';
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC <link href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/prism/1.29.0/themes/prism.min.css" rel="stylesheet" />
